{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02931",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.66,
      "end_seconds": 3.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Hi doctor, am I too early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.52,
      "end_seconds": 8.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "no problem at all, come in what's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 9.46,
      "end_seconds": 13.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.32,
      "end_seconds": 17.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "yes, that's no problem at all please sit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.61,
      "end_seconds": 21.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "It's dizziness on standing, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.79,
      "end_seconds": 26.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "how long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.5,
      "end_seconds": 34.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "I've had it for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.32,
      "end_seconds": 40.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "have you noticed any triggers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.69,
      "end_seconds": 47.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Standing definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.73,
      "end_seconds": 53.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.51,
      "end_seconds": 57.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "it just comes and goes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.5,
      "end_seconds": 61.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.64,
      "end_seconds": 79.27,
      "duration_seconds": 16.63,
      "text": "erm, it feels severe to me i've also had a widespread sunburn-like rash, for four weeks there's a sudden high fever as well i had vomiting and diarrhoea before that's settled now, though"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.25,
      "end_seconds": 83.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "okay, have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.18,
      "end_seconds": 102.0,
      "duration_seconds": 16.82,
      "text": "I had a mole taken off my arm a few years ago. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.73,
      "end_seconds": 118.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.43,
      "end_seconds": 128.58,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "It's sertraline, 50 milligrams, once a day for my mood. Propranolol, 40 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 130.21,
      "end_seconds": 138.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "doctor, I think the last prescription for the propranolol was 20 milligrams we changed it at the last visit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.0,
      "end_seconds": 144.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "right do you happen to have the the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.68,
      "end_seconds": 151.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "no, I left it at home. A tampon i take it in use"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.88,
      "end_seconds": 156.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.03,
      "end_seconds": 167.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "Yes, tramadol, it gives me feeling very drowsy. Kiwi. I come out in... well, hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.74,
      "end_seconds": 171.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.22,
      "end_seconds": 176.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.18,
      "end_seconds": 180.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.24,
      "end_seconds": 184.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.29,
      "end_seconds": 188.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.56,
      "end_seconds": 192.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.61,
      "end_seconds": 196.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Right, are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.67,
      "end_seconds": 202.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "My father had bowel cancer. My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.35,
      "end_seconds": 207.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.14,
      "end_seconds": 214.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "I've had depression for five years now. I have migraines, for about ten years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.1,
      "end_seconds": 235.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Any sore throat or stiff neck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.46,
      "end_seconds": 241.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "no, no sore throat or stiff neck"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.89,
      "end_seconds": 243.77,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "Any cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.82,
      "end_seconds": 246.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "No, no cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 247.97,
      "end_seconds": 252.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice cough. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.18,
      "end_seconds": 261.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.97,
      "end_seconds": 275.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.9,
      "end_seconds": 278.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "no changes there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.85,
      "end_seconds": 292.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.74,
      "end_seconds": 307.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.68,
      "end_seconds": 328.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 92 over 58, temperature is 36.8 degrees. And respiratory rate 20, pulse 102."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.11,
      "end_seconds": 331.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.25,
      "end_seconds": 335.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.78,
      "end_seconds": 342.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.65,
      "end_seconds": 346.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.5,
      "end_seconds": 366.83,
      "duration_seconds": 10.33,
      "text": "You are very hot, your blood pressure is low and there is a flat red rash over the body and palms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.79,
      "end_seconds": 380.89,
      "duration_seconds": 10.1,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Okay, thinking it through, this is probably possible toxic shock syndrome. I can't rule out a viral illness yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.89,
      "end_seconds": 383.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.58,
      "end_seconds": 414.54,
      "duration_seconds": 29.96,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with possible toxic shock syndrome do well once it's treated properly. Blood cultures is what I'd like next, for possible toxic shock. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'll request a vaginal swab, it'll help with possible toxic shock. I'm going to put you on flucloxacillin, 2 grams, now, single dose. That's for possible toxic shock syndrome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.12,
      "end_seconds": 444.06,
      "duration_seconds": 27.94,
      "text": "Remove any tampon, you are going to hospital now. I'd like you to see the emergency team as well, and I'll write the referral. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. We'll catch up straight away. What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 446.04,
      "end_seconds": 453.99,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "So, I take the flucloxacillin, 2 grams, now and come back straight away. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 456.0,
      "end_seconds": 460.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Right, yes, exactly right. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 462.79,
      "end_seconds": 465.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}